  "agent_descriptions": [],
  "final": "Each project row now has a Delete button. It opens a confirmation dialog, and confirming removes the row and shows a toast. I ran it in headless Chrome (Playwright) at 375px and 1280px, and both widths behaved the same.\n\n**What changed**\n- **`app.js`:** the Delete button opens the dialog, and confirming removes the project and shows the toast. The button's accessible name includes the project name.\n- **`styles.css`:** one line so the button doesn't shrink on narrow screens.\n- I reused the existing `Button`, `Dialog` and `Toast` components and the design tokens, so there is no new styling.\n\n**What I checked at each width**\n- There is no horizontal scroll, and every Delete button is fully on screen. This includes the very long unbroken project name, which wraps inside the row.\n- Cancel and Escape both close the dialog and leave all 5 rows in place.\n- Confirming Delete drops the list to 4 rows. The toast reads `Deleted \"<project name>\"`. There were no console errors.\n- I looked at the phone screenshots of the dialog and the toast. Both render cleanly. The screenshots are saved in the scratchpad.\n\n**Limitations**\n- Deletion only changes the in-memory list, so a page reload brings the project back. That fits the app, which has no backend.\n- After a delete, keyboard focus isn't moved anywhere, because the button that opened the dialog is gone.\n\nI didn't add a test to `tests/test_static.py`, and I didn't commit anything.",
